\section{Introduction}
West Albay Bikol (ISO 639-3 \texttt{fbl}) is a Bikol variety of Albay province, Philippines, spoken in a group of towns (for example Oas, Libon, Polangui) between the Rinconada area and Legazpi. Each town's speech differs noticeably. The searches found no dedicated West Albay dictionary, primer or full grammar.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
No West Albay primers or textbooks were found.

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item CUNY Graduate Center thesis with a grammatical sketch of West Albay Bikol (Balugo and Polangui dialects): \url{https://academicworks.cuny.edu/gc_etds/5781}
\item McFarland, C. D. 1974, \emph{The Dialects of the Bikol Area} (Yale dissertation), Glottolog reference record: \url{https://glottolog.org/resource/reference/id/61602}
\item Wikipedia, Bikol languages: \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bikol_languages}
\end{itemize}

\section{Religious and Community Resources}
None found.

\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Wikitongues page for West Albay Bikol: \url{https://wikitongues.org/languages/fbl/}
\end{itemize}

\section{Curriculum Development Context}
The language is described as vigorous, but no school programme in it was found. Materials for standard (Naga-based) Bikol, which is outside this survey entry, may serve as a model only. New materials would have to be written, and a town variety chosen.
\end{document}
